Privacy Notice</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c15"></span></p>=
<p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c9">If you or your end users access Read Alo=
ng via a Google Workspace for Education account this Privacy Notice will no=
t apply and the </span><span class=3D"c6"><a class=3D"c2" href=3D"https://w=
ww.google.com/url?q=3Dhttps://workspace.google.com/terms/education_privacy/=
&amp;sa=3DD&amp;source=3Deditors&amp;ust=3D1717497725632639&amp;usg=3DAOvVa=
w2-ov3JfuaLijQNqYM9k5pW">Google Workspace for Education Privacy Notice</a><=
/span><span class=3D"c3">&nbsp;or other agreement under which Google has ag=
reed to provide Google Workspace for Education will govern your use of Read=
 Along.</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=
=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c9">This Read Along privacy notice is intended to he=
lp parents understand what data is collected by Read Along and how we use i=
t. &nbsp;This notice provides information about our privacy practices that =
are specific to Read Along and summarizes the most relevant portions of the=
 </span><span class=3D"c6"><a class=3D"c2" href=3D"https://www.google.com/u=
rl?q=3Dhttps://policies.google.com/privacy&amp;sa=3DD&amp;source=3Deditors&=
amp;ust=3D1717497725632941&amp;usg=3DAOvVaw24jjYrxheQ9A7S9USTWb-E">Google P=
rivacy Policy</a></span><span class=3D"c3">.</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><=
span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Read Along =
can operate either as a signed in or signed out service. When signed in, th=
e user signs in through their Google account, and their history and prefere=
nces are saved on the account, so that they can use the service on any devi=
ce just by logging in. When signed out, the user doesn=E2=80=99t need to us=
e a Google account to sign in, but their history and preferences are saved =
on the device only. </span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span=
></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c9">Signed in service is available to b=
oth web and android app users, but signed out service is only available for=
 existing users on the android app.</span></p><h2 class=3D"c5" id=3D"h.mr7s=
if8jodvh"><span>Information we collect</span></h2><p class=3D"c0"><span cla=
ss=3D"c3">When you use Read Along, Google collects information based on you=
r children's use, like when they read a book. This information includes:</s=
pan></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><ul class=3D"c11 l=
st-kix_bjuv2hyc05zh-0 start"><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D=
"c3">log information, including usage statistics on how our service is used=
, device event information, and the device's Internet protocol (IP) address=
;</span></li><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">general loc=
ation information (such as city or state) based on your device=E2=80=99s IP=
 address; and</span></li></ul><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span>=
</p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">When using Read Along as a signed in=
 service:</span></p><ul class=3D"c11 lst-kix_bjuv2hyc05zh-0"><li class=3D"c=
0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">Google collects account identifiers fr=
om yours or your child=E2=80=99s signed-in session, used to collect and sto=
re information such as preferred language, reading history, stories you res=
trict and other settings.</span></li></ul><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D=
"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">When using Read Along as=
 a signed out service:</span></p><ul class=3D"c11 lst-kix_1klu4f753ir-0 sta=
rt"><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">Google collects a un=
ique identifier based on the device, which is used to collect and store inf=
ormation about an app or device, such as preferred language, reading and se=
arch history, and other settings.</span></li><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0=
"><span class=3D"c3">Google also uses various technologies to collect and s=
tore app activity as described above, including cookies or similar mechanis=
ms. The information collected through cookies or similar mechanisms is used=
 for the purposes mentioned below and retained for 120 days on our servers =
on a per-user basis.</span></li></ul><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3">=
</span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Both the signed in and signed=
 out services of Read Along collect voice data. The voice data is processed=
 only on the user=E2=80=99s device and is not shared with Google, to protec=
t users=E2=80=99 privacy. Voice data is not stored at all after processing.=
</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"=
><span class=3D"c9">Both the signed in and signed out services of Read Alon=
g also let users set up different profiles for their children, and let them=
 select from an array of provided avatars and set a name for their profile.=
 </span></p><h2 class=3D"c5" id=3D"h.upm207s2cqiv"><span>How we use informa=
tion we collect</span></h2><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">When using Re=
ad Along on the app or the web, Google collects the above described informa=
tion so that your child can continue progressing from session to session. I=
t allows your child to see prior reading history and keep track of in-app r=
ewards your child has earned. Prior reading history is used to recommend bo=
oks that match your child=E2=80=99s interests and reading level. This infor=
mation is essential to support your child=E2=80=99s journey over months or =
years as they build up their reading skills. </span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7">=
<span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">When using=
 either the signed in or signed out versions of Read Along, with the except=
ion of sharing to teachers or admins as described below, Google does not al=
low your children to share personal information with third parties or make =
it publicly available.</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></sp=
an></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Google also uses the information =
collected for internal operational purposes such as spam and abuse preventi=
on, enforcing content license restrictions, determining preferred language,=
 analysing usage of the signed-in or signed-out versions of the application=
, and providing, maintaining and improving the service.</span></p><p class=
=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3"=
>When using the signed-in version of Read Along, Google also offers a mecha=
nism for teachers and admins to create groups to allow multiple children to=
 share with their teacher information on which books they are reading, how =
well they are doing, and how many minutes they are reading overall, as well=
 as their name within the app. This allows the teacher to guide your child =
and the other children in the group to practice reading regularly.</span></=
p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span cl=
ass=3D"c3">When using the signed-out version of Read Along, if you would li=
ke to review and/or delete any of the data collected by Read Along that is =
stored on your device, you can do so by deleting the Read Along app, or usi=
ng your device operating system=E2=80=99s application data deletion feature=
. </span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><span class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c=
0"><span class=3D"c3">When using the signed-in version of Read Along, if yo=
u would like to delete any of the data collected by Read Along that is stor=
ed on the server against your account identifier, you can do so by clicking=
 the =E2=80=9CDelete History=E2=80=9D button from the app=E2=80=99s left na=
vigation menu. Deleting your entire Google account will also delete this da=
ta from the signed in version.</span></p><h2 class=3D"c5" id=3D"h.hx4rqty4g=
4yt"><span class=3D"c8">Information we share</span></h2><p class=3D"c0"><sp=
an class=3D"c3">Google will not disclose personal information outside of Go=
ogle unless one of the following circumstances applies:</span></p><h3 class=
=3D"c1" id=3D"h.49p24lv45o56"><span class=3D"c10">With consent</span></h3><=
p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Google will share personal information wi=
th companies, organizations or individuals (such as teachers or Admins) out=
side of Google when we have parental consent.</span></p><h3 class=3D"c1" id=
=3D"h.te0q3hosvdlw"><span class=3D"c10">For legal reasons</span></h3><p cla=
ss=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Google will share personal information with co=
mpanies, organizations or individuals outside of Google if we have a good-f=
aith belief that access, use, preservation or disclosure of the information=
 is reasonably necessary to:</span></p><ul class=3D"c11 lst-kix_2gv2ac83vdf=
z-0 start"><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">meet any appl=
icable law, regulation, legal process or enforceable governmental request.<=
/span></li><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">enforce appli=
cable Terms of Service, including investigation of potential violations.</s=
pan></li><li class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">detect, prevent=
, or otherwise address fraud, security or technical issues.</span></li><li =
class=3D"c0 c4 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c3">protect against harm to the =
rights, property or safety of Google, our users or the public as required o=
r permitted by law.</span></li></ul><h3 class=3D"c1" id=3D"h.thghuef890v7">=
<span class=3D"c10">For external processing</span></h3><p class=3D"c0"><spa=
n class=3D"c3">Google may provide personal information to our affiliates or=
 other trusted businesses or persons to process it for us, based on our ins=
tructions and in compliance with our Privacy Policy and any other appropria=
te confidentiality and security measures.</span></p><p class=3D"c0 c7"><spa=
n class=3D"c3"></span></p><p class=3D"c0"><span class=3D"c3">Google may sha=
re aggregate information about the use of the app with third parties to, fo=
r example, show trends about the use of the app or meet our reporting oblig=
ations with partners.</span></p><h2 class=3D"c5" id=3D"h.sb6phywzc8th"><spa=
n class=3D"c8">Interpretation of conflicting terms</span></h2><p class=3D"c=
